# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q statement.tex
#
# One warning is suppressed, checked hit by hit on 28 August 2026 rather
# than assumed, with a 100% false-positive rate in this file:
#
#   38  "You should not use punctuation in front of quotes." Each of the 3
#       hits is the final character of a sentence quoted verbatim from the
#       source paper. The punctuation belongs to the quoted text; moving it
#       outside the quotation marks would misquote the source.  (3 hits)
#
# Everything else stays on; the three warning 8 hits chktex raised on the
# first draft (an en-dash in "Reed--Muller", where the house style writes a
# plain hyphen) were fixed in the source rather than silenced. As of
# 28 August 2026 the file is clean under this config and
# `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n38
}
